{{Codex|Kunai throwing daggers offer a silent alternative to the traditional sidearm. Perfect for assassins.}}

The '''Kunai''' are a set of throwing knives, released in {{ver|8}}. It deals a significant amount of damage, but can be hard to aim with because of its arrow-like arc projection.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}; it is also a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Tipedo}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Bo}} + {{Weapon|Kunai}} → {{Weapon|Tipedo}}<br><small>Tipedo required for [[Lesion]]</small>
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Can hit multiple enemies in a short line (caused by flying dead bodies and not by the Kunai).
*Can use the Kunai-exclusive {{M|Stockpiled Blight}} augment.
*Has two {{Pol|Madurai}} polarity.

{{Advantages|
*[[Silent]].
*The arc of the shots enable headshots over cover.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Below average [[critical multiplier]].
*Has travel time, making it difficult to land an accurate shot at long distances.
*Shoots in an arc, making it difficult for use at long range.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Mk1-Kunai}}

==Acquisition==
The Kunai's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*The Kunai does not have the pinning properties of other projectile weapons, such as the {{Weapon|Boltor}} or {{Weapon|Paris}}, but will simply throw targets backwards upon death.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Kunai Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Kunai Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*Make sure to adjust your aim for moving targets.
*When using at a distance, aim above the enemy to adjust for the arc of the blades.
*Using the {{M|Pistol Ammo Mutation}} mod can help regain lost ammo when needed.
**Alternatively, bring along [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s.
*The Kunai's throwing arc means you can sometimes aim at targets behind cover. Aiming slightly above the cover will result in the Kunai curving downwards onto the target.
**Note that this is extremely situational, as enemy cover is usually too high to take advantage of this.

==Trivia==
*The [[wikipedia:Kunai|Kunai]] (苦無) were traditionally a multipurpose tool, similar in design to a crowbar or trowel. It could be used for gardening, masonry, and other things. Popular culture has since associated the kunai with ninjas.
*The {{Weapon|Despair}} and {{Weapon|Hikou}} share similarities to the Kunai, they are all thrown secondaries that deal mostly {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*{{ver|16.7}} revealed the Kunai to be a themed-weapon based off the {{Weapon|Paris}}, in the same manner that other themed-weapons like the {{Weapon|Akjagara}}, {{Weapon|Aksomati}}, and {{Weapon|Bolto}} are related to the {{Weapon|Tigris}}, {{Weapon|Soma}}, and {{Weapon|Boltor}} respectively.

